WEBVTT

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:01.430
Bye.

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:02.240
See you.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:15.900
Kanna-<i>chan</i>!

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.600
I'm sorry for the trouble.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.930
Don't worry about it.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.630
That fever reducer...

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:34.000
Oh, my mother used to use it.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.930
Yeah, it really works, right?

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:44.270
It was so much fun yesterday...
I got too excited.

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:48.270
You should get some rest.

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:52.080
Yes. Goodnight.

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:55.800
Night.

00:01:03.950 --> 00:01:10.500
That old bastard was giving her money
every month right until he disappeared.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.510
Where'd he get the cash?

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:20.640
"With Most Beloved"

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.570
Kanna-<i>chan</i>...

00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.270
I didn't know she could smile like that.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:30.900
Is that her sister?

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:34.250
Something's wrong here.

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:37.280
There's three rocks at Futago rock?

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:39.860
That's impossible...

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:20.720
"Episode 16: Within Unmoving Time"

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.140
Hey.

00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:27.680
Arima-<i>kun</i>? There's no classes today...

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:30.390
Yeah, I came to see you.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:36.140
You say that to all the girls, don't you?

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:40.690
I wanted to do some research
about Mt. Sankaku's history.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:43.310
I thought you might know.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:46.670
Oh, that's why.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:50.380
Here, this has anything
you might want to know.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:50.830
"A Natural History of Sakaimachi"

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:54.290
It's an awful musty book.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:58.590
Remember what Kanna-<i>chan</i>
said about the diorama we're making?

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:04.400
When I heard that, I went and looked
at the history of Sakaimachi's geology.

00:04:05.300 --> 00:04:08.640
Just what I'd expect from a history nut!

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:11.730
Don't call me a nut.

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:12.810
How about...

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:13.890
Quiet.

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.850
I haven't said anything yet.

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:19.190
I can tell what you're going to say.

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:21.410
Guess, then.

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:23.850
Let me see...

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:26.950
"Oh, Mio!

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:30.790
You are a shining goddess descending
upon the world of historical study!

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:36.420
More beautiful even than Aphrodite,
the Goddess of Love!"

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:38.640
Was that right?

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.820
No, not quite.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:48.970
Great. They came out perfectly!

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:56.900
That's him...

00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:00.820
In the chaos during and
immediately following the war,

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:04.170
there was a plan to destroy Mt. Sankaku.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:05.990
Yes.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.620
The plan was scrapped immediately.
But one of the rocks was destroyed,

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:12.330
and that's why it's called
Futago Rock, or "Twin Rock."

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:18.750
Taken in 1945...

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.420
This is definitely it!

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.800
Um...

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:27.090
You think anybody's out there who's
lived more than 50 years without aging?

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:30.510
What? Did you read that in some sci-fi novel?

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:33.010
Yeah, that's what you'd normally think...

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:39.100
I'm back! Masakatsu Yuki
has come with the pictures!

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:43.610
Oh, Boss, I just saw that stalker!

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:45.030
Hojo?

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:47.570
He disappeared into the
back alleys of Central Street.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.160
He must've been up
to something naughty again!

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:52.240
Naughty?

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:55.740
Oh, well...

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:01.730
I made it.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:08.970
Hojo-<i>san</i>, I want this to be our last time.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:10.260
What?

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:19.270
Hey, what do you think about this?

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:20.510
What?

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.020
The geology of Sakaimachi?

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:29.450
It kind of looks like a bomb went off.

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:31.160
Yeah.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:38.160
Is it possible that Sakaimachi was made
when two different things collided?

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.390
Collided?

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:44.040
Dr. Kodai Arima said something similar.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:52.390
"Authors: Kodai Arima, Ryuzoji, Imagawa"

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:46.710
In his 400 Year Cycle Theory,

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:51.550
he says that every 400 years,
different dimensions approach each other.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:56.330
If it was a collision, not an approach...

00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:59.890
Dr. Imagawa said the same thing.

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:04.400
An "event collision,"
where different dimensions collided...

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:06.780
Event collision?

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:11.780
That would explain
Mt. Sankaku's unique geology.

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:16.290
But how'd they collide?

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:18.680
Did one dimension come
falling down from the sky?

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:21.580
Well...

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:25.790
Arima, can I have a minute?

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:30.470
The last time? What do you mean?

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:32.560
I mean I won't see you anymore.

00:07:34.180 --> 00:07:38.490
Are you swearing an oath of chastity
to Takuya Arima, your new best friend?

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.730
Arima-<i>san</i> has nothing to do with this.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:46.980
Since you're always so expressionless,
it's easy to tell what you're thinking.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:54.140
What would he think if he knew
what you've done in your life?

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:59.500
All right. This will be our last time.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:04.380
But in exchange,
tell me where Dr. Kodai Arima is.

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:11.380
I know that you were his lover.

00:08:11.380 --> 00:08:17.690
Tell me the truth. Or I'll make it
so you can never go to school again.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:19.890
School...

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:25.620
It'll be the same as before.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:29.500
I'll just repeat the same thing as always.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:32.030
Hey, what are you saying?

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:33.650
Hey, you!

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:38.620
What's all this about?

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.450
Um, well...

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:44.290
My daughter's being a rebellious teenager.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.500
I was yelling at her.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:46.530
Your daughter?

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.570
You two don't look anything alike.

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:54.590
Let's go home, daughter.

00:08:56.840 --> 00:09:00.470
I see. So Hatano-<i>kun</i> collapsed again.

00:09:00.470 --> 00:09:03.410
The fever reducer worked, at least.

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:07.980
By the way, where is
Shimazu-<i>kun</i>'s vacation home?

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.440
The next town over.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:12.940
You can't swim here because
of the Geotech construction project.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.820
Outside Sakaimachi, huh?

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:16.300
I knew it.

00:09:17.110 --> 00:09:22.290
I'm glad she's safe.
I was right to put it in your hands.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:25.330
About that... Why me?

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:30.000
A teacher's intuition, maybe?

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.880
Intuition?

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:35.050
I have a pretty high opinion of you.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.300
You do?

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.180
Did you discover my secret ability,

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:41.260
where I can discover the location
of your nipples just by looking at them?

00:09:42.140 --> 00:09:43.560
Oww.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:46.390
I mean the way you try
to get close to anybody,

00:09:46.390 --> 00:09:50.650
regardless of common decency or etiquette.

00:09:50.650 --> 00:09:53.610
Then let me ask you,
without regard for common decency...

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:56.030
Does Kanna-<i>chan</i> not have a parent
or somebody to look after her?

00:09:56.030 --> 00:10:00.120
They're overseas.
And we can't get a hold of them.

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:05.330
There's a lot about her I don't understand.

00:10:05.330 --> 00:10:07.300
Her school transfer record, for example.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:12.540
She's gone from one school
to another, not just in Sakaimachi,

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:18.550
but the next town over,
and the town next to that.

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:21.890
That's not that rare, is it?

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:24.520
The problem is the
number of times it's happened.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:25.810
Number of times?

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:29.240
Just the stuff I can
find records for shows that

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:32.710
she's transferred schools over 20 times.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:35.820
"School Withdrawal Form"
"Student Name: Kanna Hatano"

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:57.090
Hey. How you feelin'?

00:10:57.090 --> 00:11:00.090
I was in a good mood until I met you.

00:11:01.010 --> 00:11:03.100
I haven't introduced myself yet, have I?

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:06.180
Here's my card.

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:07.770
I don't want it.

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:09.480
Don't say that.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:14.060
I know that. But you don't know me.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.170
That's not fair.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:20.740
"Atsushi Hojo
Tagata Detective Agency"

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:20.740
"Space Detective McDumbass."

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:22.990
That's not what it says.

00:11:23.120 --> 00:11:26.990
So what does some guy from
a detective agency want with me?

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:29.620
I was hoping I could get your help.

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:31.000
Help?

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:38.550
As near as I can tell, only Kanna
Hatano knows where Dr. Arima is.

00:11:40.300 --> 00:11:44.430
Is my dad still alive somewhere?

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:46.980
He is.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:53.100
Dr. Arima was paying
her bills for almost a year.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:55.450
She's his lover, actually.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:00.530
If you knew that already,
we can get right to the point.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:03.240
How about we make a deal?

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:06.530
I don't think that's happening.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:09.120
I guess you don't like me.

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:12.850
There's no "guessing" about it.
I don't like you.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:18.380
Don't you want to know where your dad is?

00:12:18.380 --> 00:12:19.670
Hey!

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:23.680
Hey, you! What's all this fuss--

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:25.590
You again?

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:30.850
I was just having a fight with my son...

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:35.700
Coming!

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:41.110
Good morning.

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:44.660
My name is Hatano,
and I'm one of Arima-<i>san</i>'s classmates.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:47.150
He lent me this hat...

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.360
He did?

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:56.630
Arima-<i>kun</i>, your classmate, 
Hatano-<i>san</i>, is here!

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:58.250
Come in!

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:00.130
No, I'll be going...

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.720
What's up, Kanna-<i>chan</i>?

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:04.560
I came to give you back your hat...

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:10.920
Your classmates are all cute girls, huh?

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.640
Is she the one you're really after?

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:18.080
Um... Ayumi-<i>san</i>, I'll be back later.

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:19.430
Let's go.

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:23.480
Come back any time, Hatano-<i>san</i>!

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:33.130
The birds are chirping.
The water in the fountain is sparkling.

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:37.330
If this isn't peace, what is it?

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:39.730
It may seem that way, yes.

00:13:41.090 --> 00:13:41.920
You don't agree?

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:46.350
The birds never know
when a predator will attack them.

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:51.930
And the fountain is just an indulgence
for humanity's destruction of nature.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:58.210
Our lives exist on top
of a very fragile balance.

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:00.440
You've got a point.

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:03.610
It's not just "a point." It's the truth.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:05.900
The truth, huh?

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:12.000
Kanna-<i>chan</i>, can I ask a weird question?

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:13.360
Yes.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:19.100
I told you that I saw someone
with that pendant when I was a kid, right?

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:24.600
She looked the same and
was the exact same age as you.

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:29.630
While I'm asking something strange...

00:14:30.390 --> 00:14:33.330
Was that you?

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:44.570
If he doesn't have a collar, is he lost?

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:46.030
There's a lot of that going, lately.

00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:53.120
I guess dogs prefer cute girls, huh?

00:14:53.990 --> 00:14:57.040
Puppies just don't judge people
based on appearance, that's all.

00:15:02.330 --> 00:15:06.170
If I could live like a puppy,
I'd be really happy, I bet.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:13.850
No anger, worries, or 
sorrow, or loneliness...

00:15:13.850 --> 00:15:18.770
I think anger and sorrow are
part of what makes life worth living.

00:15:20.310 --> 00:15:25.860
That's something people who haven't
experienced true anger or sorrow say.

00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:35.430
I'm tired of being betrayed and hated.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:46.590
I've never met someone like you, Arima-<i>san</i>.

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:47.840
Really?

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:55.840
I want to know more about you.
I want to hear more about you.

00:15:57.310 --> 00:16:00.730
There's no point in telling you about me.

00:16:00.730 --> 00:16:04.610
Isn't it normal to want
to know more about your friends?

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:09.140
Friends? With me?

00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:13.160
Yeah, Mio and Yuki feel that way too.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:15.030
As do I.

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:22.210
You can be very cruel, Arima-<i>san</i>.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:25.720
Goodbye.

00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:42.360
Hey.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:45.350
I'm getting tired of you, Mr. Detective.

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:48.860
Don't call me that. It's rude.

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:51.360
Show me some respect.

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:53.820
Why don't you leave us alone?

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:56.490
Who the hell is paying you?

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:58.150
I can't tell you.

00:16:58.870 --> 00:17:01.290
So about that deal...

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:08.250
Both you and I want
to know where Dr. Arima is.

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:16.930
I'm not asking for a lot.
Just leave this in Kanna's room.

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:20.090
A bug...

00:17:21.390 --> 00:17:26.270
It's not a bug. It's a "listening device."

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:31.780
That thing's expensive!

00:17:31.900 --> 00:17:33.780
Sorry.

00:17:33.780 --> 00:17:36.660
Send the bill to your employer.

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:39.910
If you don't help me,
something awful will happen!

00:17:42.160 --> 00:17:43.870
Shit!

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:45.790
Hey, you.

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:50.310
I think you need to find
a new way of raising your kids.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:53.800
I'll work on that.

00:17:56.430 --> 00:17:59.440
You've gone past your deadline.

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:03.350
Kanna Hatano is refusing to talk,

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:07.560
and Dr. Kodai Arima's son
is being uncooperative.

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:08.310
Is that so?

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:13.840
My other agent is doing
quite good work, however.

00:18:16.450 --> 00:18:21.120
If I can get a little more time,
I can get you the information you want.

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:25.890
If I can isolate Kanna, to the point
where there's no one she can rely on...

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:30.330
Look into my eyes.

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:32.230
I'm sorry?

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:46.930
So the rumor was true.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:49.400
She's such an ordinary-looking girl, too...

00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:52.440
--You never can tell with people, huh?
--What's this about?

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:56.400
"The Wild Sex Life of Kanna Hatano"

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:06.450
I see.

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:09.390
So that's why you've
transferred to so many schools.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:12.650
Are you going to do the same thing this time?

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:16.410
Eventually you'll have no
place to go, even in Sakaimachi.

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:23.950
I never had a place to go in this world.

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:30.270
It's the same for you, right Takeda-<i>sensei</i>?

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:38.320
"The Wild Sex Life of Kanna Hatano"

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:38.820
What the hell is this?

00:19:38.820 --> 00:19:40.240
What are you doing?

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:41.950
You can't just tear it down!

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:45.830
This is what you do with gossip like this.

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:47.450
"The Wild Sex Life of Kanna Hatano"

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:47.450
Wait!

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:50.370
You're violating their freedom of expression!

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:52.500
Freedom of expression...

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.210
...belongs to people who

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:56.610
can put their names down and
take responsibility for what they say!

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:58.510
Right, Boss?

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:00.760
Y-Yeah...

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:05.300
I don't know who did this,
but this is a terrible thing to do!

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:09.480
But there's all those weird
rumors about Hatano-<i>san</i>...

00:20:09.480 --> 00:20:11.390
Stop spreading rumors, you guys!

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:16.400
How would you feel
if someone did this to you?

00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:18.140
Just imagine it!

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:26.190
That was great, Mio.

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:30.370
We're lucky that this
happened over summer break...

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:32.100
But who would do this?

00:20:34.250 --> 00:20:37.340
"School Withdrawal Form"
"Student Name: Kanna Hatano"
"Reason: Family Reasons"

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:36.890
Kanna-<i>chan</i>'s transferring?

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:38.750
That's right.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:40.840
She had all the paperwork ready to go.

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:45.340
I told you that she'd done this before.

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:47.900
But when I looked into all those transfers,
I found something out.

00:20:48.850 --> 00:20:54.900
She's only transferring
to schools around Sakaimachi.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:21:04.210
Essentially, she's been transferring schools
in a circle around Sakaimachi.

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:05.740
Kanna-<i>chan</i>...

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:07.990
Why is she doing that?

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:12.370
We can assume there's some reason
she needs to stay near Mt. Sankaku,

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:16.100
and also a reason she has
to keep transferring schools.

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:21.530
That's why I asked you to look after her.

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:25.470
You've noticed, haven't you?

00:21:25.470 --> 00:21:30.040
Her secret is deeply
connected with your parents.

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:33.040
She went home.

00:21:33.650 --> 00:21:36.440
You know what you have to do, right?

00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:40.160
Yeah.

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:41.530
"Episode 17: A Pale, Ephemeral Vow"

00:23:35.850 --> 00:23:39.430
Episode 17: "A Pale, Ephemeral Vow."
